      "id": 1,
      "text": "Millerton's location was originally known as Chula, which means fox in the Choctaw language.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=MI034"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Wheelock Church, located near Millerton, is the oldest church building in Oklahoma.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millerton%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Millerton was platted and formed in 1907 between an old military trace and the railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=MI034"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1908, the Miller Lumber Company in Millerton shipped more than 250 cars of finished lumber.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=MI034"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Millerton sits on high ground that drains south toward Buzzard Creek and north to Wheelock Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millerton%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
